For our client located in BRUGES, we are looking for a ROOFER.

Do you enjoy working at heights and do you have experience as a roofer, mainly working on pitched roofs? Then we are looking for you!

As a ROOFER in the Bruges region, your day will look like this:

• Mainly covering pitched roofs, but occasionally also flat roofs;
• Renovating existing roofs (no new-build projects);
• Installing roofing materials;
• Assessing the structural characteristics of existing roofs;
• Installing and sealing carpentry elements in the roof;
• Bonding and installing EPDM.
As a ROOFER in BRUGES, you have the following qualities:

• You have solid work experience as a roofer, with experience working on pitched roofs;
• You have a category B driving licence;
• The starting location is Bruges, Blauwe-Toren area;
• You speak Dutch or English;
• You are not afraid of heights.

To further grow our Modern Data Platform Practice, we are currently looking for a skilled Power BI Expert.

Do you have at least 3 years of experience in designing and building data solutions with Power BI? You want to further develop your abilities & knowledge by working together with highly skilled, helpful and fun colleagues? You are not afraid to be challenged intellectually and personally?

If so, send us your CV and we’ll contact you for an interview and a cup of coffee.


Your responsibilities 
• You’re able to work independently on a Power BI assignment;
• Analyze user requirements and design business intelligence solutions;
• Model the data according to business and technical requirements;
• Perform data analysis and generate insights;
• Create visualizations and dashboards;
• Actively participate in knowledge building and sharing;
• Stay up to date with new features and releases in Power BI (and Fabric);
• 
Communicate findings and insights effectively to stakeholders.



Your qualifications 
• A minimum of 3 years of experience in speaking with and understanding the needs of clients;
• Between 3 and 5 years of experience with visualization tools such as Power BI and/or Tableau and/or Qlik and/or Looker;
• Experience with DAX, Power Query and SQL
• Hands-on experience with data modeling;
• Knowledge of best practices in Power BI for both data visualization and VertiPaq internals;
• Familiarity with ETL processes and data warehousing concepts;
• Fluent in Dutch and/or French and English;
• Strong communication and interpersonal skills;
• Problem-solving abilities and attention to detail.

Your growth path 
• Further grow our Modern Data Platform Practice;
• Continuous learning on projects as well as through training;
• Participate in knowledge building through our competence centers;
• Gradually, you’ll assume more responsibility and grow to a coaching role for more junior colleagues

For our client, a family-owned construction and transport company that has been active since 1940, we are looking for a C/CE Truck Driver.

This family business, where a passion for construction has been passed down from father to son, specialises in construction works, the sale and transport of building materials, and earthworks.

As a C/CE Truck Driver (concrete mixer or truck-mounted crane), your responsibilities will include:

• Driving a concrete mixer truck or a truck equipped with a truck-mounted crane and transporting concrete and building materials to various construction sites;
• Starting your working day at the company’s premises or from home (provided you have a safe place to park your truck) and ensuring timely deliveries to construction sites;
• Driving and operating your truck safely and correctly;
• Following the work schedule and respecting agreements with customers;
• Ensuring the proper maintenance and cleanliness of your truck;
• Complying with all safety regulations on the road and at construction sites.
As a BUILDING MATERIALS TRUCK DRIVER CE, you recognise yourself in the following profile:

• You have a valid C/CE driving licence, professional competence and CODE 95;
• You have experience as a truck driver;
• Experience driving a concrete mixer truck is an advantage, but motivation and willingness to learn are just as important;
• You are flexible and have no problem starting work early in the morning;
• You communicate well in Dutch or English;
• You treat your truck, customers and colleagues with respect;
• You are looking for a stable job in a family-owned company.
Interested in this vacancy? Contact us at westkust@absolutejobs.be.
